+# Data for /sell/net-proceeds/ (batch 2026-11-a)
+
+Every number on the page comes from `findings.json`, which `build_findings.py` builds. Ledger: Blog-Brain `batches/2026-11-a/sell-net-proceeds/facts.md`. No MLS numbers, map points, addresses or names are kept here. The raw listing pull (MLS numbers, prices, points) stays in scratch: `wf2/sell-net-proceeds/raw/listings-net-proceeds.json`.
+
+| File | What | Made by |
+|---|---|---|
+| findings.json | The page's numbers: costs by price tier, the worked net sheet, the tax proration example, the withholding example, deed fees paid in 12 months, owners by tax-bill state, homes for sale with a price cut or a home warranty | build_findings.py |
+| listings.json | Homes for sale now inside the Census Horry County outline: price cuts and home warranties, by type and price band (counts only) | pull_listings.py |
+| raw/google-suggestions.txt | Google search suggestions for 49 searches | pull-suggestions.sh |
+| raw/src/ | Copies of the primary sources read: SC Code 12-8, 12-24, 12-43, 12-45, 27-1, 27-30, 27-31, 29-3; CFPB Reg Z 1026.36 and the payoff answer; IRS Pub 523 and the 1099-S instructions; Horry County treasurer and register of deeds pages | curl. SC Realtors Form 310 is copyrighted, so its PDF and text stay in scratch (`wf2/sell-net-proceeds/priv/`); the ledger quotes the lines used. |
+
+Inputs reused from siblings (not copied):
+- `data/2026-10-d/sell-home-value/findings.json` (county_all: resale prices) and `raw/horry-county.json` (county outline).
+- `data/2026-10-d/sell-out-of-state-buyers/out-of-state-buyers.json` (13,194 recorded home sales, Oct 2025 to Sep 2026) and `raw/stock-by-state-condo.json`, `raw/stock-by-state-house.json` (owners by tax-bill state).
+
+To rerun (RAW = a scratch folder outside the repo):
+
+```
+sh pull-suggestions.sh > raw/google-suggestions.txt
+RAW=$RAW HORRY=../../2026-10-d/sell-home-value/raw/horry-county.json python3 -I pull_listings.py .
+python3 -I build_findings.py <website repo root>
+```
