+/* /sell/net-proceeds/ - what a seller keeps after selling a house in Horry County: the worked net sheet on the
+ * county's middle $350,000 home, the calculator, who pays what on South Carolina's standard contract, deed stamps by
+ * price, the mortgage payoff, the property tax split at closing, HOA charges, the hold-back for sellers who live out
+ * of state, how sellers here keep more of the price, and the tax on the gain.
+ *
+ * Batch 2026-11-a, Lane U. Version 1. The live page was hand-made; this spec replaces it.
+ * Facts: Blog-Brain batches/2026-11-a/sell-net-proceeds/facts.md, VERIFIED rows, and CORRECTED rows only in the
+ * verifier's wording (VERIFY.md). Struck wording: sell-net-proceeds-struck.json (no "9/2023"; no "costs ... $1,320"
+ * without "a mortgage to release"; "most homes outside city limits"; no "long-time owner ... usually"; no "sellers
+ * paid $18 million"; no "builder's offer, not a seller's habit"; no "condo owners" for tax-bill addresses).
+ * Data, never typed (website working copy):
+ *   data/2026-11-a/sell-net-proceeds/findings.json   tiers (rows 8, 11, 13, 14), the tax split (rows 17 to 19), the
+ *                                                    hold-back (row 28), deed stamps in a year (row 12), tax bills
+ *                                                    mailed out of state (row 29), listings (rows 34, 35)
+ *   data/2026-11-a/sell-net-proceeds/verify-recount.json   the verifier's listing count; the page's listing figures
+ *                                                    must agree with it (rows 34, 35)
+ *   data/2026-11-a/buyers-cost-to-own/hoa-horry.json  houses and condos for sale with no HOA fee (row 26, CTO's values)
+ * Sources: SC REALTORS Form 310 (03/2026); SC Code 12-24, 8-21-310, 12-45-70, 12-43-220, 27-1-70, 27-31-200 and
+ * -220, 12-8-580; CFPB; 12 CFR 1026.36; IRS Pub 523, Topic 701, 1099-S instructions; HUD 4000.1; VA; NAR; Horry County
+ * deeds, parcels and 2026 levy; Chapter3 CRM active listings counted in aggregate (no MLS sold data).
+ * Kept from the live page: the calculator (rebuilt: no unsourced default, the tax split and the hold-back added), the
+ * lead form with its consent text word for word (source "net-proceeds"), the phone number, the deed stamp rule, the
+ * links to capital gains, home value, FSBO and closing costs, and the FAQ questions readers search.
+ * Corrected from the live page: the owner's title policy is the buyer's (row 2); the hold-back is the buyer's duty and
+ * is on the gain only with the affidavit (row 27); "requires an attorney to conduct closings" (row 9); the three
+ * untested tips are replaced by our listing counts (rows 34, 35); "the same day" is out (owner question Q6).
+ * Owner questions still open (facts.md): Q1 the seller's attorney fee (the line shows no number and the calculator box
+ * starts empty), Q2 the example commission (5 percent, labelled an example), Q3 local HOA fees (no figure), Q5 when
+ * sellers get paid (left out).
+ * Built by tools/mkpage.js. */
